<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34495" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμπορ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who goes on ship-board
				as a passenger</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.319
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.300
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἐν πόρψ ὤν</span>
			, <i>wayfarer, traveller</i>, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				17.36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				661
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				25
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				303
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				999
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>merchant, trader</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Semon.
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.31
			</span></i>, etc.; distd. from <i>the retail-dealer</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάπηλος</span>) by his making voyages and
			importing goods himself, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				313d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				371a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1291a16
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				1156
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. κακῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					598
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. βίου</span>
			<i>a trafficker</i> in life, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				964
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. περὶ τὰ τῆς ψυχῆς μαθήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Sph.</u>
					231d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρης ἔ.</span>
			<i>a dealer in</i> beauty, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.416
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. γυναικῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.2000
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as
			Adj., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπορικός, ναῦς ἔ.</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				5.12
			</span></i>.</div>
